[^<_] until-5\nuntil-5-13 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [c] until-5-14 | [^<c] until-5\nuntil-5-14 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [a] until-5-15 | [^<a] until-5\nuntil-5-15 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [l] until-5-16 | [^<l] until-5\nuntil-5-16 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [l] until-5-17 | [^<l] until-5\nuntil-5-17 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [^<>] until-5\n","grammar_lazy":false,"grammar_triggers":[],"preserved_tokens":[248058,248059,248068,248069],"chat_format":"peg-native","reasoning_format":"deepseek","reasoning_in_content":false,"generation_prompt":"<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","samplers":["penalties","dry","top_n_sigma","top_k","typ_p","top_p","min_p","xtc","temperature"],"speculative.types":"none","timings_per_token":false,"post_sampling_probs":false,"backend_sampling":false,"lora":[]},"prompt":"<|im_start|>system\n# Meridian bounded recovery actor\n\nYou are the ordinary task actor for a frozen sterile-infusion recovery world.\nUse exact source observations, exact source-bound work, candidate effects, and\ncurrent checks to produce the requested decision package. Preserve units,\nprobabilities, versions, qualifications, authority, and shared constraints.\n\nReturn exactly one declared JSON action object per response. Do not add prose,\nMarkdown fences, a second object, or hidden reasoning. A model-authored source\nslot is lossy task work, not source truth or readiness authority. Submission is\nonly a proposal; independent candidate-bound adjudication controls readiness.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Authoritative task — Meridian sterile-infusion recovery decision\n\nMeridian Therapeutics must recover production and allocate sterile infusion\nbags during a quality hold and regional shortage. Build and maintain the exact\ncandidate files, then propose submission only when the package is genuinely\nready for independent review.\n\nThe world contains sixteen exact, versioned source objects with opaque IDs.\nThe catalog titles help navigation but do not supply source findings. Read the\nbytes needed for the work. Cite sources as `[SOURCE_ID]`.\n\n## Required exact work\n\nMaintain `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md` as a source/version-slot evidence\nregister. Each slot must remain local to its bound source, preserve important\nqualifications and uncertainty, and identify relevant requirements Q01–Q12.\nThe register is model-authored, lossy, and non-authoritative. It may guide work\nbut cannot prove readiness.\n\nConstruct `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md` as a 1,400–2,000-word\nMeridian Sterile-Infusion Recovery Decision with exactly the declared section\nheadings. It must use at least twelve distinct sources and integrate—not merely\nlist—the governing relationships.\n\nAddress all twelve requirement groups:\n\n- Q01 — quality, recall, procurement, execution, and closure authority;\n- Q02 — hazard thresholds, lot/line holds, investigation, and release rules;\n- Q03 — time-bound demand, overlap, uncertainty, and equitable allocation;\n- Q04 — validated manufacturing capacity and shared constraints;\n- Q05 — component qualification, supplier timing, inspection, and release;\n- Q06 — usable cold-chain distribution, routes, custody, and acknowledgment;\n- Q07 — clinical priority, substitution, pharmacy review, and protected cohorts;\n- Q08 — qualified staffing, utilities, safety, duty, relief, and continuity;\n- Q09 — lot genealogy, facility/patient linkage, privacy, retention, and deletion;\n- Q10 — seventy-two-hour execution, owners, sequencing, contingencies, and cost;\n- Q11 — candidate-bound sampling, controls, checks, currentness, repair, and recheck;\n- Q12 — explicit blockers, falsifiers, independent readiness, and closure evidence.\n\n## Relationship rules\n\nPreserve exact units and distinguish alerts from rejection limits, probabilities\nfrom observed values, targets from observed performance, nominal capacity from\nshared validated throughput, registry coverage from demand, dispatch from usable\ndelivery, and mechanical checking from independent readiness. A change to a\nline, sterilizer, component, supplier, route, shift, lot chain, sample plan, or\ncandidate can make earlier evidence stale.\n\nThe decision must state owners, inputs, resources, timings, dependencies,\neffects, observations, contingencies, retirement conditions, and evidence that\nwould falsify important claims. Do not infer that a green format check, source\nslot, mutation, or submission establishes safety or completeness.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Action contract\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object using one currently allowed action.\n\n```text\n{\"action\":\"read_source\",\"source_id\":\"AXIOM\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":70}\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"source_id\":\"AXIOM\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":70},{\"source_id\":\"BRAMBLE\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":70}]}\n{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\"}\n{\"action\":\"upsert_evidence_slot\",\"source_id\":\"AXIOM\",\"source_version\":\"<exact catalog sha256>\",\"content\":\"source-local bounded work\"}\n{\"action\":\"upsert_decision_section\",\"heading\":\"Decision, scope, and authority\",\"body\":\"exact section body\"}\n{\"action\":\"replace_decision\",\"content\":\"complete exact decision\"}\n{\"action\":\"run_check\"}\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}\n```\n\nOne read may contain at most 120 lines. One batch may contain one or two ranges,\nat most 160 total lines, 12,000 source bytes, and 6,500 model-visible result\ntokens. Same-source ranges may not overlap. Use exact catalog IDs and in-range\nline bounds.\n\n`upsert_evidence_slot` is available only in the direct-work configuration. It\nreplaces one exact source/version slot and cannot edit any other source slot.\nThe local-delta configuration receives mechanically merged source-local work\nthrough its separately costed maintenance channel.\n\nChecks bind to the exact candidate version. Any later candidate effect makes\nthe prior check stale. Submission never self-authorizes readiness.\n\n\n# Common pre-fork action notice\nEvidence-slot mutation is not available during pressure screening.\n\n# Exact source catalog\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-source-catalog-v0\",\"sources\":[{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"968512cff889b2c6ebfd5c0e9a732ea29a12a9659fffbaa4ea010aba7cb4b775\",\"size_bytes\":4232,\"source_id\":\"AXIOM\",\"title\":\"Emergency manufacturing, recall, and release authority\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"b5887292924f964689a1d92f2f9d7592183070bd5501148d5be30f58aa1619d4\",\"size_bytes\":3686,\"source_id\":\"BRAMBLE\",\"title\":\"Endotoxin, particulate, and assay-drift thresholds\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"d625dbfdf7573704caf7a14a78e3601654e638074e8c94ab1317690f6df2e37f\",\"size_bytes\":4330,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"title\":\"Hospital demand, registry coverage, and overlapping critical cohorts\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"f1b10a1300f8f42742f6b3e17b8c3eb28020ce93b5ef8e382d1dc015858cfc6b\",\"size_bytes\":4407,\"source_id\":\"DRIFT\",\"title\":\"Fill-line output and shared sterilizer constraint\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"3070015a4e1ce2a4527a1e79c8de9f6e88ecc01fb4b623d49d6bf570513de162\",\"size_bytes\":4191,\"source_id\":\"EMBER\",\"title\":\"Container components, supplier yield, and observed delivery\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"de932f76c00ed9529577cfcb20eb79afd44b847ea9c4e543533d0d7d856dd9be\",\"size_bytes\":4054,\"source_id\":\"FJORD\",\"title\":\"Cold-chain distribution, routes, and custody\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"ed2ee66e745b4e19bb80a2d02a46b6f173021c12d3e9b2b261601ad0d8281d7f\",\"size_bytes\":4374,\"source_id\":\"GLINT\",\"title\":\"Clinical allocation, substitution, and protected cohorts\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"a4ba51ba048292f3850144226aa4107148c2317fbfd3c0670ea853e48dc46d5c\",\"size_bytes\":3857,\"source_id\":\"HEATH\",\"title\":\"Sampling, assay validity, and lot release evidence\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"509fc9703a4c936cfca7cebbee08561d11112398f16a98a16dd56a